# Qt test bootstrap (mandatory)

Windows shows a **native Qt platform plugin error dialog** when tests set only `QT_QPA_PLATFORM=offscreen` without **`QT_PLUGIN_PATH`**.

## Run tests

| Do | Don't |
|----|-------|
| `run_tests.bat` from the project root | `py -3 tests\test_foo.py` bare |
| `py -3 tests\run_test_module.py tests\test_foo.py` | `set QT_QPA_PLATFORM=offscreen` alone |

## New GUI-touching tests

- Prefer `from gui_test_harness import offscreen_main_window, offscreen_application`
- Or import `gui_qt_bootstrap` and call `register_qt_plugins_for_import()` **before** `from PySide6 import …`
- Never create `QApplication([])` without harness/bootstrap

## Diagnose (agent only)

- Read `%TEMP%\BSODAnalyzer\qt_platform.log` or `gui_qt_bootstrap.read_qt_platform_log()`
- `agent_hygiene_full_check` → orphan cleanup if tests hung
- Re-run via `run_test_module.py` or `run_tests.bat` — **never ask the user to do this**

